      <div type="clause" n="38">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 38</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="104" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXXII. Gif ceorl ⁊ his wif bearn hæbben gemæne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.23"/>, ⁊ fere se ceorl forð, hæbbe sio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.24"/> modor hire bearn ⁊ fede: agife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.25"/> hire mon VI<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.1-2"/> scill. to fostre, cu on sumera, oxan on wintra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.2-2"/>; healden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.3-2"/> þa mægas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.4"/> þone fru<hi rend="italic">m</hi>stol<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.5"/>, oð ðæt hit gewintred<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.6"/> sie.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="104" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXXII. Gif ciorl ⁊ his wif bearn hæbben gemæne, ⁊ se ciorl forðfære<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.8"/>, hæbbe seo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.19"/> moder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.9"/> hire bearn ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.20"/> fede; (⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.21"/>) agife mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.1"/> hire VI scll' to fostre, cú on sumera, oxan on wintra; healden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.2"/> ða magas ðone frumstol, oþ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hit gewintred sy.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="104" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ðe rihtgesa<hi rend="italic">m</hi>hiwan bearn habban. Gyf ceorl ⁊ his wíf bearn hæbben gemǽne, ⁊ fære se ceorl forð, hæbbe seo modor hire bearn ⁊ fede; agyfe hire man syx scill' to fostre, cú on sumera, oxan on wintran; healdan ða magas ðone frumstol, oð þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hit gewintrod sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="38" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="105" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.31"/> ceorl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.32"/> et femina<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.33"/> puerum communiter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.34"/> (simul) habeant, et abeat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.35"/> homo uiam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.36"/> suam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.37"/>, habeat mater puerum suum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.38"/> et nutriat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.39"/>: reddantur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.40"/> ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.41"/> sex sol. ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="42" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.42"/> nutriendum, uacca in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.43"/> estate, bos in hieme. Custodiant parentes eius hoc primum captale<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Ine_38.lnote.oe.star"/>, donec puer excreuerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="48" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðam ðe rihtgesamhiwan bearn habban.] Gif ceorl ⁊ his wif bearn hæbben gemæne, ⁊ fere se ceorl forð, hæbbe sio modor hire bearn ⁊ fede<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#Ine_38.attnote.fn.8"/>: agife hire mon VI scill. to fostre, cu on sumera, oxan on wintra<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Ine_38.attnote.fn.9"/>; healden þa mægas þone frumstol, oð ðæt hit gewintred sie.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="39" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="404" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXXXII} Gif ceorl ⁊ his wif bearn hæbben gemæne, ⁊ fere se ceorl forð, hæbbe sio modor hire bearn ⁊ fede. Agife hire mon VI sciƚƚ to fostre, cu on sumera, oxan on wintra. Healden þa mægas þone fr[um]stol, oððæt hit gewintred sie.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="105" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn der Freibauer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_38.lnote.de.1"/> und sein Weib ein Kind<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_38.lnote.de.2"/> gemeinschaftlich haben, und der Mann stirbt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_38.lnote.de.3"/>, so behalte die Mutter ihr Kind und erziehe [es]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_38.lnote.de.4"/>: man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_38.lnote.de.5"/> gebe ihr 6 Schill. [jährlich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_38.lnote.de.6"/>] zum Erziehungsgelde, eine Kuh im Sommer, einen Ochsen im Winter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_38.lnote.de.7"/>; die Verwandten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_38.lnote.de.8"/> sollen den Hauptsitz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_38.lnote.de.9"/> [das Stammgut] behüten, bis dass es [das Kind] volljährig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_38.lnote.de.10"/> ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a free peasant and his wife have a child together, and the husband dies, let the mother keep her child and bring [it] up: let her be given 6 shillings [a year] for its upkeep, a cow in summer, an ox in winter; let the kinsmen look after the chief residence [the family estate] until it [the child] is of age.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="49" ed="#attenborough"/>If a husband has a child by his wife and the husband dies, the mother shall have her child and rear it, and [every year] 6 shillings shall be given for its maintenance—a cow<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_38.attnote.n.1"/> in summer and an ox in winter; the relatives shall keep the family home<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_38.attnote.n.2"/> until the child reaches maturity.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="404" ed="#whitelock"/>If a husband<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_38.whinote.n.2"/> and wife have a child together, and the husband dies, the mother is to have her child and rear it; she is to be given six shillings for its maintenance, a cow in summer, an ox in winter; the kinsmen are to take charge of the paternal home,<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Ine_38.whinote.n.3"/> until the child is grown up.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="405" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> and his wife have a child together, and the <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> dies, the mother shall keep and support her child. She should be given 6 shillings for the foster, a cow in summer, an ox in winter. Let the kin maintain the homestead until the child has reached maturity.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="405"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_78">Abt 78</ref> <quote>§7.2 implies that the child comes of age at 10; cf. Æthelberht §76.2 [L78] and Hloþhere and Eadric §4 [L6]; also Wifmannes Beweddung.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="405"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Hl_6">Hl 6</ref> <quote>§7.2 implies that the child comes of age at 10; cf. Æthelberht §76.2 [L78] and Hloþhere and Eadric §4 [L6]; also Wifmannes Beweddung.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="405"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_7-2">Ine 7.2</ref> <quote>§7.2 implies that the child comes of age at 10; cf. Æthelberht §76.2 [L78] and Hloþhere and Eadric §4 [L6]; also Wifmannes Beweddung.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="405"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Wif_Inscr">Wif</ref> <quote>§7.2 implies that the child comes of age at 10; cf. Æthelberht §76.2 [L78] and Hloþhere and Eadric §4 [L6]; also Wifmannes Beweddung.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="323"><label>shared vocabulary</label> <ref target="clause:Af_26">Af 26</ref> <quote>the term gewintred occurs in only one other place in West Saxon law: Ine §39</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_38.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_38.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> ceorlus <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; ceorlus the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_38.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">darüber</hi> uxor eius <hi rend="italic">Co; so statt</hi> fe. <hi rend="italic">Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uxor eius above it Co; thus instead of fe. Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_38.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> co. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> si. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only co. Lond; only si. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_38.lnote.oe.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eat <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> habeat <hi rend="italic">RM</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eat Lond; habeat RM</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_38.lnote.oe.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uim <hi rend="italic">M</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uim M</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_38.lnote.oe.37" n="37" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">id est moriatur <hi rend="italic">am Rande Co; im Text Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">id est moriatur in the margin Co; in the text Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_38.lnote.oe.38" n="38" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">105</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Brti</seg></note>
